--- valid: scalar present in the same row ---
{"a":42,"a":{"b":43}}
{"a":42,"a":{"b":43}}
--- valid: destination declares a typed path below, so the parser descends ---
{"a":0,"a":{"b":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":0,"x":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":0,"x":1}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":{"c":1}}}
{"a":0,"a":{"b":{"c":1}}}
--- valid: sibling path that only shares a prefix ---
{"a":0,"ab":1}
{"a":0,"ab":1}
--- valid: the new typed path is a scalar in the source ---
{"a":1}
{"a":1}
--- valid: no rows, so nothing is read and nothing raises ---
--- type_json_skip_invalid_typed_paths drops the data below the typed path ---
{"a":0}
{"a":0}
{"a":0,"z":9}
{"a":0,"z":9}
{"a":42,"a":{"b":43}}
{"a":0}
{"a":42,"a":{"b":43}}
{"a":0}
{"a":0}
{"a":0}
